# Rare Granite & Twin Cities: Inside Milano Cortina 2026

## Headline: The Granite Secret & A Tale of Two Cities

- **The Island of Stones:** Did you know that every single curling stone used in the Olympics is made from a unique type of granite found only on a tiny Scottish island called **Ailsa Craig**? This rare stone is water-resistant and incredibly tough, ensuring it doesn't crack when sliding on the ice.

- **A Historic First:** Milano Cortina 2026 marks the first time in Olympic history that two cities are officially named as co-hosts. While Milan brings the urban vibe and fashion, Cortina d'Ampezzo offers the breathtaking beauty of the Dolomites. It’s a perfect blend of "City and Mountain."

